# Accessibility rules

A11y is non-negotiable. Treat it like type safety: encode it, run it in CI, fail PRs that regress.

## Every interactive control

- `accessibilityRole` set explicitly: `'button'`, `'link'`, `'image'`, `'header'`, `'switch'`, `'checkbox'`, `'radio'`, `'tab'`, `'menuitem'`.
- `accessibilityLabel` set — never rely on visible text alone for icon-only controls.
- `accessibilityState` for stateful controls: `{ disabled, busy, checked, expanded, selected }`.
- `accessibilityHint` only when the action is non-obvious from the label (rare; lean on better labels first).

## Tap targets

- **Minimum 48×48 dp** for all interactive elements.
- For visually smaller targets (e.g., a 24-px icon button), set `hitSlop={8}` (or larger) so the tappable area expands.

## Live regions

Use `accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"` for:
- Form validation errors (so VoiceOver announces them as they appear)
- Toast/banner status changes
- Loading-state captions ("Loading posts…", "Submitting…")

`"assertive"` only for genuinely interrupting messages (rare).

## Color and contrast

- Text contrast ratio ≥ **4.5:1** against its background (WCAG AA). Use the semantic tokens — they're tuned for AA.
- Never communicate state with color alone. Pair with an icon, label, or pattern.

## Reduced motion

Respect `useReduceMotion()` from `react-native-reanimated`. Decorative animations should disable, not just shorten, when reduce-motion is on.

## Screen structure

- One `accessibilityRole="header"` per screen at the top of meaningful content.
- Lists: ensure each item has a complete accessibility label (e.g., for a post item: `"{{title}}, posted by {{author}} on {{date}}"`).
- Don't break visual reading order with absolute positioning if it changes accessibility tree order.

## Focus management

- Modals and bottom sheets: focus the title on open, restore focus to the trigger on close.
- After navigation, the screen header should be the first focusable element.
- Use `AccessibilityInfo.announceForAccessibility('…')` for transient announcements after async actions.

## Forms

- Each field has a visible label (or `accessibilityLabel` on the input).
- Errors are announced via `accessibilityLiveRegion` on the error `<Text>`.
- `aria-invalid={Boolean(error)}` on the input. (Already wired in `<TextField />`.)
- Group related fields with `accessibilityRole="form"` (rare in RN; native handles this).

## Testing

- `getByRole` / `getByLabelText` queries in RTL doubles as a11y audit.
- Maestro a11y flows live in `.maestro/flows/a11y/`. CI runs them nightly.
- Manual QA: enable VoiceOver (iOS) / TalkBack (Android) and walk through every user-facing flow before release.
